            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for to bury, then the Persian for a grave."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ختم",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ختم (khatm) — \"a memorial gathering\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مراسم ختم در مسجد برگزار شد. Marâsem-e khatm dar masjed bargozâr shod. The memorial service was held at the mosque."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A gathering soon after a death, often at a mosque. khatm first means \"a completion\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "khatm is usually traced to Arabic khatm, \"a sealing, a completion\", as of a reading of the Quran for the dead. EtymDB lists the Persian word with no parent."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
