              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "عزا ('azâ) — \"mourning\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "خانواده یک هفته عزا داشتند. Khânevâde yek hafte 'azâ dâshtand. The family were in mourning for a week."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "'Azâdâr \"a mourner\"; black clothes are worn in 'azâ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "'azâ is borrowed from Arabic 'azā', \"solace, mourning\" (EtymDB)."
